					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1637482#post-2809038</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1637482/labyrinth-s-end#post-2809038</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 03 May 2017 04:08:50 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Sebsk</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2764406</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I'm flabbergasted.</p> <p>You have a great mind.</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Final&nbsp;thoughts/feedback</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Thank&nbsp;you.</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <blockquote> <p>there is of course no threat of alien invasion. That's a joke.</p> </blockquote> <p>Is it supposed to be ambiguous whether he means that an alien invasion is a joke, or that he's joking about there not being any threat?</p> <blockquote> <p>without scientific proof, all we have is empty conjecture</p> </blockquote> <p>I feel like these are not the words of someone that has insight to what actually happened here would say; limiting yourself to &quot;proof&quot;, which as a term in itself never (by any and all current understanding) can fully be conclusive (ref. &quot;methodologies&quot;), would mean that he's trying to actually <em>separate</em> humanity from this &quot;entity&quot; for as long as possible, which in turn would mean he has actually not insight into what actually transpired.</p> <p>Is this the intention?</p> <p>Many regards, great, awesome, and incredible(!) work, sorry to have these two issues at the end! I am honestly really amazed at your skills and inner workings creating this. Many many kudos.</p> </div> </div> </div> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
