					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1637482#post-2469353</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1637482/labyrinth-s-end#post-2469353</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 08 Mar 2016 08:52:20 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>psul</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2156983</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>It's hard to know what more can be said about this - not much needs to be said to anyone who has read it. Attempting to write about peace, and consciousness, and the infinite, comes with a very high degree of difficulty - especially to end a story on that note. For me, this avoids narm and feels expansive; it almost captures that vertiginous feeling of sudden understanding. Very good work.</p> <p>Two really small things:</p> <blockquote> <p>the edges of the universe as understood by their charges centuries-long efforts to document the cosmos</p> </blockquote> <p>As the efforts belong to the charges, should that be <span style="text-decoration: underline;">charges'</span>?</p> <blockquote> <p>Initial explorations of the site have not uncovered evidence of any specific alien lifeforms that may have constructed.</p> </blockquote> <p>Constructed <span style="text-decoration: underline;">it</span>?</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
